{% from '_time.j2' import ago, ahead -%}
# The cast.  Names are the usual cryptographic-protocol crowd, because
# they already carry roles: mallory is the one who attacks, peggy is the
# one who proves things.
#
# Timestamps are Jinja2 -- ago(days=400) and friends, from _time.j2 --
# rendered when the seed is loaded, so the aged accounts stay aged
# however long this material sits on a shelf.  The margins are chosen so
# the seed still works up to about three weeks after it was rendered:
# carol has 20 days left inside a 30-day warning, ivan starts in a
# month.  Every password is "<uid>-pw".
#
#   alice    healthy, changed yesterday          the control case
#   bob      changed 400 days ago                expired under pwdMaxAge
#   carol    changed 345 days ago                inside pwdExpireWarning
#   dave     has not logged in for 200 days      pwdMaxIdle
#   erin     flagged as reset by an admin        pwdReset / pwdMustChange
#   frank    locked by an admin, permanently      pwdAccountLockedTime
#   grace    an administrator                    group-based assignment
#   heidi    HAS NO PASSWORD AT ALL              require_password
#   ivan     starts next month                   pwdStartTime
#   judy     left last month                     pwdEndTime
#   mallory  fresh and expendable                the brute-force target
#   oscar    password stored in the clear        hashing / rehash
#   peggy    fresh                               history and quality
#
# employeeType is staff for everyone except carol and peggy, who are
# contractors -- stage 5 targets a policy with a filter on it.

dn: uid=alice,ou=people,{{ suffix }}
objectClass: inetOrgPerson
uid: alice
cn: Alice Ahmed
sn: Ahmed
